      "id": "map-and-streaming",
      "note": "map fields with both a message value and a scalar value (only the message value produces a `uses` edge — a scalar is a keyword, not a reference), and all four rpc streaming combinations. The grammar gives an rpc's request and response the same node type with no field name, so this case is what proves they are told apart by position and that `stream` is read off the tree.",
